    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="11" relname="background">My article seemed similar to what you are describing in regards to body movement.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="16" relname="span">It made me think that we have intuitiveness as a physical reflex and as a cognitive process.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="15" relname="contrast">A physical reflex would be a person interacting with others in the game you described.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="15" relname="contrast">A cognitive process would be where someone knows how the rules of physics works and makes some great deduction based on this knowledge.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="14" relname="span">Both would be based on experience</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="condition">if success is achieved,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="13" relname="contrast">but one happens much quicker than another.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="12" relname="contrast">One requires quick interaction</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="12" relname="contrast">and one allows for time to ponder on inherent rules (laws of physics) that dont change.</segment>
        <group id="10" type="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="multinuc" parent="17" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="13" type="multinuc" parent="16" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="13" relname="contrast"/>
        <group id="15" type="multinuc" parent="2" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
    </body>
